 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2496) '- Status: `zpool status` reads ONLINE with no errors, and `zfs get` reads back each option.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2496) '- Readback: a 200 MB compressible file and a 50 MB random file hash the same before and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2496) '  after `sync`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2496) '- Compression: the test dataset held 243 MB and took 49.7 MB, a ratio of 4.90x. The random
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2496) '  file takes its full size, so a ratio near 1.00x on it is the control.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2496) '- Case: writing `a.txt` after `A.txt` leaves one file whose content is the second write.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2496) '  That is the wanted result on a case-insensitive pool, and a pool that keeps two files
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2496) '  fails the check.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2496) '- Scrub: `zpool scrub` repairs 0 bytes and reports 0 errors.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2496) '- Table: `diskutil list` shows the data partition as type ZFS and a second 8.4 MB ZFS
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-16T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2496) '  reserve partition, and no FAT or EFI partition remains.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2496  1 LINE
 Text:Written

